{"availability":"available","full":"maxgfr/unmark","name":"unmark","description":"Find, decode and remove watermarks in your browser: invisible Unicode and steganography in text, C2PA/EXIF/XMP metadata in files, and visible image watermarks via exact unblending or AI inpainting. Nothing is uploaded.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-14T14:37:25Z","updated":"2026-10-10T17:44:24Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://maxgfr.github.io/unmark/","topics":["agent-skill","c2pa","exif","inpainting","local-first","metadata","onnx","privacy","provenance","pwa","steganography","unicode","watermark","watermark-removal","watermark-remover","zero-width"],"demo":"https://maxgfr.github.io/unmark/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:14.205Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:14.205Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:14.205Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:14.205Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["maxgfr.github.io/unmark — find, decode and remove watermarks and provenance marks, in your browser or from your terminal.","Invisible characters in text. Metadata in files. Watermarks drawn into images. Every mark is named, located and graded before anything is stripped, and what cannot be removed is stated on the screen that does the removing. Located literally: click a finding and the cursor lands on the character it found, in a view that draws the invisible ones so there is something to look at.","Several good open-source projects each solve part of this, and none runs in a browser: watermarks-remover covers text Unicode hygiene and container metadata in Python, watermark-removal covers visible image watermarks with TensorFlow and a GPU, and unslop is the sharpest thing written on detecting generated prose — its three-layer split and its eval contract are both borrowed here, with credit. All of them ask you to inst